Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Goldberg-Palatini Cubic Comparison with CLM", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"e6076596-7525-4d4c-a2d6-25820154c589"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook derives the quadratic and cubic second-order Lagrangians from \
the first-order Goldberg-Palatini bootstrap kernels and compares them with \
Capper, Leibbrandt and Ramon Medrano (CLM), Phys. Rev. D 8, 4320 (1973), Eqs. \
(2.10) and (2.16). The inverse of M0 is derived here rather than imported. \
The cubic comparison is an exact local equality after matching conventions; \
the quadratic comparison includes an explicit total derivative. No separate \
momentum-space vertex extraction is performed.

Keep this notebook beside Goldberg_Palatini_Bootstrap_kernels.wl and evaluate \
the input cells in order in a fresh kernel with xAct/xTras installed. \
FeynCalc is used by the exporting notebook, not by this calculation. Use a \
separate kernel if the bootstrap notebook is running concurrently.

The normalization is that of Eq. (5.1) and Eqs. (6.1)-(6.3) of the \
accompanying article. The dimension remains symbolic, in the generic d >= 4 \
domain of the bootstrap basis. The inverse requires d != 2; the original \
first-order expressions also contain 1/(d-1). No field equations for phi, \
gauge fixing, or on-shell restrictions are imposed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a0851ab5-bf9b-4abd-87da-7382f114a200"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1) Packages", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"28daff3f-a812-4f9e-ab4e-97ae974e147a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

